{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794785312,"nonce":"TnmudyHuoPuK/+QY3CA+KzOoIgI=","title":"Scrolling to an image stalls a window while it decodes","message":"User report: scrolling past a section with images stalls the scroll briefly. Window trace (cn_demo, release-debug) showed render-phase spikes of 87 ms and 47 ms at the scroll offsets where the avatar section came near the viewport.\n\n`preload_images` loaded each image inline in the frame that first needed it: `ImageData::load` (cn_demo's avatar.jpg is 6.3 MB) and then `GpuImage::from_rgba_maybe_compressed`, whose BC encode is documented at 50-150 ms per 2K texture, inline.\n\nFix: `RenderContext::set_async_image_decode(true)` (on for desktop windows) hands the whole load, decode, compression and upload to a worker thread (`context/image_decode.rs`); the frame draws the placeholder or nothing, the window keeps drawing while one is underway (`has_pending_image_fade`), and the first frame after it arrives is a full paint that draws it. Headless rendering keeps loading inline so goldens see images on their first frame; wasm loads inline.","files":null}]}